{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra","id":1068676,"title":"Slaugh / Lasombra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-27T08:11:04-07:00","id":1068676,"title":"Slaugh / Lasombra","content":"In a mixed game would Slaugh and Lasombra 'Shadows/Abyss' ever crossover? I'm asking for a friend, so I hope someone understands what they are asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Tiffany Sanderson<br /> HBN = HP + OWOD +CoC = <a href=\"http://www.hogwartsbynight,com\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.hogwartsbynight,com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13156-toreador4ever","name":"toreador4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T08:28:38-07:00","id":1068685,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, no. The classic world of darkness games are intended to be their own separate settings (meta plot, not withstanding). Vampires may exist within Changeling and Changelings may exist within Vampire, but they're not the same kind of Vampires / Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T08:35:36-07:00","id":1068688,"title":"","content":"Excellent, I'll let my players know they can't cross over. If those things are separate things then I'll keep them apart. I just have a Lasombra in my game doing shadow tricks in front of a confused Slaugh and they weren't sure quite how to react.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Tiffany Sanderson<br /> HBN = HP + OWOD +CoC = <a href=\"http://www.hogwartsbynight,com\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.hogwartsbynight,com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13156-toreador4ever","name":"toreador4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T09:14:39-07:00","id":1068703,"title":"","content":"They went back and forth on whether the games were part of the same setting or not.<br /> <br /> As re your question, the shadows the sluagh are familiar with are natural shadows, the shadows under the bed, the shadows outside the window, the shadows of the deep dark woods. Obtenebration and the Abyss is... outside context for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T09:46:48-07:00","id":1068717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>toreador4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra?p=1068688#post1068688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent, I'll let my players know they can't cross over. If those things are separate things then I'll keep them apart. I just have a Lasombra in my game doing shadow tricks in front of a confused Slaugh and they weren't sure quite how to react.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Been watching videos talking about WoD recently and they brought up that the mechanics from each game line don't blend well with the other games. For example, a point of strength in werewolf is more / less effective than a point of strength in vampire, and so on. So they're meant to be played separately; Chronicles of Darkness is another story, though.<br /> <br /> The only major thing that seems to connect them all is the meta plot in which all the different game lines have some manner of involvement. But mechanically, it's difficult to pull off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-27-2017, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T10:13:23-07:00","id":1068730,"title":"","content":"Check out the Kiasyd chapter in Lore of Bloodlines. It ties the Thallain to the Abyss in ways that ought to be good fodder for Vampire/Changeling crossover chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T12:11:11-07:00","id":1068786,"title":"","content":"I cross over in my games all the time, though I mainly use one line as my major and pull from the others. Mages make good allies, vampires good enemies, and you certainly hope that werewolf becomes your friend!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T19:47:23-07:00","id":1068991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadryx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra?p=1068786#post1068786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cross over in my games all the time, though I mainly use one line as my major and pull from the others. Mages make good allies, vampires good enemies, and you certainly hope that werewolf becomes your friend!</div> </div> </div> </div>As do I. The mythologies don't mix? Of <i>course</i> they don't mix, any more than Buddhism and Norse paganism mix. I don't even try, anymore, to make it all jive. The truth is ultimately unknowable, as there's always one more layer of secrets to peel back. Even demons could be deluded. It's like how Marvel has every pantheon be real, despite the <i>vastly</i> cosmologies.<br /> <br /> It's all true. It's all a lie. Who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T00:04:40-07:00","id":1069166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra?p=1068991#post1068991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As do I. The mythologies don't mix? Of <i>course</i> they don't mix, any more than Buddhism and Norse paganism mix. I don't even try, anymore, to make it all jive. The truth is ultimately unknowable, as there's always one more layer of secrets to peel back. Even demons could be deluded. It's like how Marvel has every pantheon be real, despite the <i>vastly</i> cosmologies.<br /> <br /> It's all true. It's all a lie. Who knows?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that is how I fit Call of Cthulhu into a harry potter and OWOD mixed game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Tiffany Sanderson<br /> HBN = HP + OWOD +CoC = <a href=\"http://www.hogwartsbynight,com\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.hogwartsbynight,com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13156-toreador4ever","name":"toreador4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T02:38:25-07:00","id":1069213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra?p=1068991#post1068991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As do I. The mythologies don't mix? Of <i>course</i> they don't mix, any more than Buddhism and Norse paganism mix. I don't even try, anymore, to make it all jive. The truth is ultimately unknowable, as there's always one more layer of secrets to peel back. Even demons could be deluded. It's like how Marvel has every pantheon be real, despite the <i>vastly</i> cosmologies.<br /> <br /> It's all true. It's all a lie. Who knows?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> DC had all the pantheons be real, too, but then all the pantheons except the Greeks wiped each other out and a new pantheon (the New Gods) emerged from the aftermath of their war. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T02:49:48-07:00","id":1069217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra?p=1069213#post1069213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DC had all the pantheons be real, too, but then all the pantheons except the Greeks wiped each other out and a new pantheon (the New Gods) emerged from the aftermath of their war. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not been the case since... at least the New 52, if not before. According to The Multiversity, all of Earth's pantheons co-exist in Skyland, in the Realm of the Gods. The New Gods have their own domains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T19:10:45-07:00","id":1070432,"title":"","content":"Which is why I prefer Marvel's take on the Gods...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T09:19:30-07:00","id":1070691,"title":"","content":"I've always thought the cosmologies fit together quite well if you just ignore who they say really runs everything. You have The One at the top, which is pure Prime, and was shattered into The Shining Ones, who are probably the Avatars of humanity or became the Avatars of humanity after further devolution. Somewhere below The One, or adjacent to It, is the Triat, which embodies each aspect of the Metaphysical Trinity and moderates (or is supposed to moderate) creation through Dynamism, Stasis and Entropy--except it was corrupted/unbalanced, skewing things. Beneath the Triat are the Celestines and Incarna, including some delusional being who thinks of himself as Jehovah and created first the angels then the vampires. No one likes him and he's way too self-aggrandising.<br /> <br /> The antithesis of The One is The Other, which might just be Oblivion or perhaps the Qlippoth, and the antithesis of The Shining Ones are the Malfeans, who embody destruction in the same way The Shining Ones embody creation. The Dreaming, meanwhile, is an isolated chunk of the Umbra which feeds off human subjectivity and the collective unconscious, and all its critters spring from the minds of sentient beings. They may once have had an independent existence like any other being of the Umbra, but now they're dependent on the dreams of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T09:21:12-07:00","id":1071293,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys for so many replies! I've passed on what was discussed to my players!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Tiffany Sanderson<br /> HBN = HP + OWOD +CoC = <a href=\"http://www.hogwartsbynight,com\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.hogwartsbynight,com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13156-toreador4ever","name":"toreador4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T07:42:27-07:00","id":1071712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra?p=1070691#post1070691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought the cosmologies fit together quite well if you just ignore who they say really runs everything. You have The One at the top, which is pure Prime, and was shattered into The Shining Ones, who are probably the Avatars of humanity or became the Avatars of humanity after further devolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>And already, you've shackled everything to Mage. Because while Mage can explain everything, it isn't unique in the WoD for being able to do this. All the games can explain everything, but never without bias, and Mage comes with substantial bias about what is and how it came to be, just like the other games. If you wanted to leave this portion out, you'd have to make what amounts to an entirely new setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T11:47:13-07:00","id":1071769,"title":"","content":"I usually use Mage as the &quot;core&quot; setting and the other splats are different but interacting paradigms. This won't work for everyone's games, but it has worked fairly well for mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T16:37:54-07:00","id":1071839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra?p=1069217#post1069217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not been the case since... at least the New 52, if not before. According to The Multiversity, all of Earth's pantheons co-exist in Skyland, in the Realm of the Gods. The New Gods have their own domains.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> DC's Skylanders!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T17:24:09-07:00","id":1071843,"title":"","content":"Didn't think this thread would go from Umbra to Skylanders, but hey, that's cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Tiffany Sanderson<br /> HBN = HP + OWOD +CoC = <a href=\"http://www.hogwartsbynight,com\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.hogwartsbynight,com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13156-toreador4ever","name":"toreador4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T19:28:15-07:00","id":1072312,"title":"","content":"You can mix everything...there are crossover books and crossover rules, but it doesn't work well without adjustments. I think the idea of not doing it it's the best from the point of view of simplicity. It's the path of less resistance.<br /> <br /> The problem it's not much if (how) the world makes sense. That's an issue we have in the community, but you can ignore the issue in the game, as characters usually aren't capable of discovering the truth behind these mysteries anyway)<br /> The problem it's that, because the authors created each game to stand on it's own, and focused the brainstorming within the confines of their game, the rules of each game aren't very compatible. There's going to be times where you will have to patch one thing or another (like, say, Disciplines that are resisted by Virtues that the other games don't have). Nedless to say, the games aren't balanced in any way (As in, a starting character from one line can trash big bosses or whole parties of another exploiting these unbalances).<br /> <br /> That being said, I think the biggest issue mixing Changeling with everything else it's the &quot;dual reality&quot; in which changelings live. When the Lasombra sees the Sluagh, he may see just a human kid!. And why would the vampire care about the Dreaming or Dreaming business?. One needs to solve these issues, to make a common ground where there's usually none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T05:14:51-07:00","id":1072461,"title":"","content":"This is also why we try to stress that the Magical Council signed a treaty to keep the different societies separated and they should only interact if it makes sense. We monitor new creations to catch the nuances as they come up and adjust the worlds as necessary so it makes less impact on them. We also cut vampiric powers down to everyone starts at level 5 of ONLY their three in-clan disciplines and werewolves can only begin with one power each up to level 3. It sounds harsh, but it has balanced rather well. <br /> <br /> The slaugh and the Lasombra are in a place where they can run into each other, but so far they RP wisely enough to not interact or go poking the bear like they should be in our setting. I'm lucky enough to have some extraordinarily good and responsible players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Tiffany Sanderson<br /> HBN = HP + OWOD +CoC = <a href=\"http://www.hogwartsbynight,com\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.hogwartsbynight,com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13156-toreador4ever","name":"toreador4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T08:52:28-07:00","id":1073153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra?p=1071712#post1071712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And already, you've shackled everything to Mage. Because while Mage can explain everything, it isn't unique in the WoD for being able to do this. All the games can explain everything, but never without bias, and Mage comes with substantial bias about what is and how it came to be, just like the other games. If you wanted to leave this portion out, you'd have to make what amounts to an entirely new setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which other settings can fit every other splat's creation myths in? Mage lets everything work all at once. Demon's tries to, and meshes well with Mage's, so one doesn't preclude the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:02:56-07:00","id":1073163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra?p=1073153#post1073153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which other settings can fit every other splat's creation myths in? Mage lets everything work all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only under Mage's way of making something work. So it's not much different than any other games' explanations for what goes on in other games. Mage isn't a grand and all-encompassing vision meant to unify all WoD games. It has its own pitfalls and needs, first and foremost to make its game about bizarre explanations for reality that don't mesh with other games work. Anything else is secondary, or lower, as a priority.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demon's tries to, and meshes well with Mage's, so one doesn't preclude the other. </div> </div> </div>Again, Demon only works for Demon, as Demon's priority is to facilitate the setting and atmosphere of Demon. It doesn't do anything else particularly well, except perhaps for Vampire, and big surprise there that the two games that go for Biblical literalism end up having their setting assumptions mesh well together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T13:31:13-07:00","id":1073335,"title":"","content":"Indeed.<br /> <br /> Mage, Demon and Werewolf are the games that put the greatest emphasis on an overarching cosmogony. All of these explain how all things work pretty much from the Basic, and the expand on that on each book. Thus, they have the greatest incompatibility. Others have more leeway about what makes the universe work, usually placing some punctual limitations that you have to work arround.<br /> <br /> Another problem it's Theme. Changeling isn't terribly uncompatible with anything (as long as you respect the methaphysics of the Dreaming), but it's theme may enter in conflict with, say, Vampire. Vampire want's to conspire, earn power, and do other banal stuff, while the Changeling want's to fight for an ephemeral glamorous ideal and live adventures in fantasyland. It's not hard to see how they may not see each other a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T13:47:39-07:00","id":1073343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra?p=1073335#post1073335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed.<br /> Another problem it's Theme. Changeling isn't terribly uncompatible with anything (as long as you respect the methaphysics of the Dreaming), but it's theme may enter in conflict with, say, Vampire. Vampire want's to conspire, earn power, and do other banal stuff, while the Changeling want's to fight for an ephemeral glamorous ideal and live adventures in fantasyland. It's not hard to see how they may not see each other a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>While on the whole I agree, I think each group would have some members who would mix more easily wiht another, for example, members of Unseelie noble houses or the Shadow Court could do very well in a Vampire story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5462-kendaan","name":"Kendaan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T15:14:09-07:00","id":1073393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kendaan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1068676-slaugh-lasombra?p=1073343#post1073343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While on the whole I agree, I think each group would have some members who would mix more easily wiht another, for example, members of Unseelie noble houses or the Shadow Court could do very well in a Vampire story.</div> </div> </div> </div>A better comparison would be vampires who unwisely throttle their unlives up to the max and burn themselves out... and most any changelings. Rather than a slow damnation or redemption that takes some time to play out, the descendants of the fae go for broke with what they do and generally prefer to burn out or explode before the wonder in their lives ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}